{
  "sealed_utc": "2026-11-23T18:23:53.237136+00:00",
  "study": "Independent visible whole-bay and lane challenge",
  "scope": "AI visual reference by an independent reviewer of original, existing public UAE driver-view photographs, no human adjudication and no legal or on-road judgement. Each image comes from a different recording. Annotation coordinates are in the exact source raster. Only the visible extent of the selected bay is traced, clipping occlusion and the image boundary.",
  "sampling": "Six primary recordings were absent from the earlier public frontage, manually marked-point, owner-check and fine-tap test photo lists. Four supplemental recordings have earlier point/frontage use but fresh whole-bay annotations. All ten are outside the preceding specific restaurant and four-photo manual challenge. Images belong to the existing public bank and the point-tap and natural-language tasks here were written before testing the candidate. Earlier development use in different tasks is not evidence of corpus-level novelty.",
  "scoring": {
    "whole_bay": "A normal selectable proposal plus point inside the matching reference polygon (boundary included), original-coordinate outline with IoU >=0.45, >=0.70 precision (fraction of predicted area inside the bay), and >=0.50 coverage (fraction of reference covered). When any bay is requested use the largest IoU among preregistered bays. Record point-only, missing geometry or a different unannotated possible bay separately; none earns whole-bay credit. Report polygons and bounding rectangles separately; score a genuine displayed rectangle geometrically if and only if it meets the same thresholds.",
    "unique_boundary": "A divider shared with an occupied bay and a visible bay mouth with no other adjacent parking target identify one vacant bay. The highlight may move inside this bay. Record the displacement from the tap in original pixels.",
    "ambiguous_shared_stripe": "A boundary shared by two vacant neighbouring bays must ask the passenger to distinguish the two specific possibilities (e.g. nearer/farther or labelled visual choices), without unilaterally offering one, or display two independently selectable distinct bay outlines. A generic retap, safety message, missing outline for a unilateral proposal, or silent guessing fails this endpoint. Score the first response then test the specific choice if available.",
    "withhold": "Ordinary completed outcome with no point or confirmable proposal. Report provider/timeouts separately, do not credit them as abstentions. Every scene includes a through-lane or travel-aisle tap.",
    "independence": "Give automatic requests typed as exact original strings with ordinary automatic submission and no passenger marks. Score manual taps in independent sessions, using the regular direct-mark page flow. No future observations, recorded user speech, or private inputs. Each offered result must still require a separate confirmation; a user mark never counts as an automatic finding."
  },
